# NOTE: pipeline/models/ (cnn_model.pt, class_names.json, metrics.json, the
# plot PNGs) is intentionally NOT ignored here and IS committed to git.
# That's a deliberate choice, not an oversight: this model is baked into
# the Docker image at build time (see pipeline/Dockerfile), so every clone
# of this repo needs to already have a trained model in it -- otherwise
# every `docker build` (or fresh teammate checkout) would need to retrain
# from the full dataset just to get a working image. After running
# `python train.py`, `git add pipeline/models` and commit/push the result
# like any other source file.

# The dataset (12,000+ images) is already ignored by the root .gitignore's
# `pipeline/data` rule -- this is a REDUNDANT, belt-and-suspenders copy of
# that same rule, scoped here in case the root rule is ever accidentally
# edited or dropped. It should never actually be "the only thing" keeping
# the dataset out of git; if it ever is, fix the root .gitignore too.
data/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Testing / Training Images
data
